B.ahu=new A.cw("source_innate","Innate","The character can use the ability as much as they like, using a Source value of {Half Power}. If the feature only has the innate source gain +1 to the source value.","If you only have innate as your only source, gain +1 to skill results.","Next scene gain +1 to skills you're proficient in, or next situation start with {Power + Level} shield.","You have -1 to attacks and proficient skills.","{Half Power}",B.F0,!1,null,null,B.f1,null)
B.F3=new A.mq(5,"minion")
B.ahW=new A.bp("Pawns","Instead of a normal chump, you have {Their Vitality} Pawns with 1 HP each. Whenever they gain shield they gain 1 shield, blocking 1 attack. If they have spectral or gain Resistance to all, they instead have 2 HP.",!1)
B.air=new A.bp("Melee","HP {4 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] Make a Melee Attack vs Str targeting 1 enemy range 1. On Success, deal {Half points d8} damage.",!1)
B.ai6=new A.bp("Range","HP {3 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] Make a Ranged Attack vs Dex targeting 1 enemy range 6/12. On Success, deal {Half points d6} damage.",!1)
B.ahJ=new A.bp("Repair","HP {2 * Level * Their Vitality}. Repair [Minion] Make a status check targeting an adjacent Ally. On Success: Heal {Half points d8}.",!1)
B.ai9=new A.bp("Shielding","HP {2 * Level * Their Vitality}. Shield [Minion] Make a status check targeting a range 1 ally. On success, they gain {Half points d6} shield.",!1)
B.ahN=new A.bp("Familiar","HP {3 * Level * Their Vitality}. [Minion] You may target your abilities and skills from your minion's space. When you do, gain a +1 to the result of attacks, skills or status checks.",!1)
B.a52=s([B.ahW,B.air,B.ai6,B.ahJ,B.ai9,B.ahN],t.AJ)
B.aht=new A.cw("source_companion","Companion","Your Companion is another character who takes their turn at the same time as you. When you trigger abilities of this source, your companion performs the ability using their stats with a source value of {Half Level}. If you do not trigger an ability of this source using your [Action] on your turn, your companion may trigger their [Minion] ability. You may have multiple companions with dm approval, treating each as a separate source.\nWhen you gain a companion, build a chump of your level but without a chump action, or combat features. Your companion has a Body Composition and Body Size but doesn't gain any bonuses related to the Body Composition or Body Size. Pick one of the below companion options, which changes the companion's Max HP.\nCompanions do not have turns but act during your turn. Companions are characters for the purposes of effects. Companions have reactions, and can concentrate. They may move up to their speed on each of your turns. If you perform a [Run] or [Retreat] your companions also take the action.","When you fail a skill or defense check, you may have your companion make the check instead. You may do this {points} times per Story.","Your companion starts next situation with {Level * Their Vitality} Shield.","Your companion has a -1 to check results.","{Half Level}",B.F3,!1,null,null,B.a52,"{1}")
B.p8=new A.mq(7,"inventory")
B.aip=new A.bp("Huckable","Increase range of abilities by {Level/3}",!1)
B.ai_=new A.bp("Dangerous","Target all characters range 1 of any of the targets and deal {Level/3 d6} damage to them.",!1)
B.aid=new A.bp("Dampening","Target all enemies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and reduce their shields by {Level/3 d6}.",!1)
B.aiq=new A.bp("Energizing","Target all Allies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and they gain {Level/3} speed until the end of their next turn.",!1)
B.ahU=new A.bp("Empowering","Allies targeted by the ability deal {Level/3} d6 extra damage on their first attack they succeed on each turn.",!1)
B.ai4=new A.bp("Protective","Target all allies range {Level/3} of any of the targets and give them {Level/3 d6} shields.",!1)
B.aio=new A.bp("Regenerative","Target all allies range 1 of any of the targets and heal them {Level/3 d10}.",!1)
B.ahS=new A.bp("Unstable","Before using the ability make a create check, on success gain a source mod of 1, on failure lose health equal to your create level.",!1)
B.a55=s([B.aip,B.ai_,B.aid,B.aiq,B.ahU,B.ai4,B.aio,B.ahS],t.AJ)
B.ahH=new A.cw("source_craft","Craft","The character gains their powers from consumable creations that they make during combat. At the start of your turn, make a create check, on success gain 1 ingredient. When using an ability, the character must spend 1 ingredient, gaining its effects and a source of {Power}. For every 4 points of this source, the character gains 1 ingredient type from below, minimum 1. Whenever you spend an ingredient, the ingredient's type effect is added to the ability's effect. If the ability requires success, the effect only occurs if you succeed. You start each encounter with 1 ingredient of each type you know. You may create with 1 free hand. You cannot concentrate on the abilities of this source. When an ability would call for concentration, instead make a status check on the start of each of the target\u2019s turns, on failure the effect ends for the target.\n[Action] gain {Half Power} ingredients of your choice.\n[Reaction] When you fail a status effect check against a target within range 6, spend your reaction and an ingredient to cause the check to succeed instead.","After you succeed on a skill check, gain 1 craft and pick a skill check. You and your allies can use the craft to gain advantage on that type of check. You may do this up to {points} times each Story. You do not gain crafts for a check in which you used a craft.","Start the next situation with 2 ingredients of each type you know and have a +1 to create checks to create ingredients.","You start the next situation with no starting ingredients and have a -1 to create checks to create ingredients.","{Power}",B.p8,!1,null,null,B.a55,"{points / 4}")
B.p7=new A.mq(6,"transformation")
B.ahZ=new A.bp("Melee","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, target an enemy range 1 and deal {points /2 d12} Damage.",!1)
B.ai5=new A.bp("Ranged","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, target an enemy range 4 and deal {points /2 d10} Damage.",!1)
B.aie=new A.bp("Elusive","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Your movement doesn\u2019t provoke attacks and you gain {points /2} Speed until the end of your turn.",!1)
B.ahP=new A.bp("Barrier","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Gain {points /2 d10} Shield and until the start of your next turn, allies range 2 may spend your shield when taking damage. On Problems, allies range 2 may spend your shield when taking damage until the start of your next turn.",!1)
B.ahT=new A.bp("Regenerative","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Heal {points /2 d6}.",!1)
B.aih=new A.bp("Armored","When you Succeed on an attack or check using your action, Gain a +1 to defense results and resistance to {points /3} defenses until the start of your next turn. When you pick this, pick the defenses. On Problems, you gain only the resistances.",!1)
B.a5a=s([B.ahZ,B.ai5,B.aie,B.ahP,B.ahT,B.aih],t.AJ)
B.ahv=new A.cw("source_form","Form","The character gains their power through altering their form. Once per situation, you transform into your alternate form before you activate one of your form source powers and remain changed as long as you are concentrating. You may only use this source when concentrating on your form, using a source value of {Power}. While in a form, you may concentrate on up to {Power} additional effects. When you lose concentration on your form, you lose concentration on these additional effects.\nWhen you choose this, pick a new body size, composition and defense class which replace your character's while in the form. When you pick your form, pick one of the below effects.\nYou may have multiple different forms, each different form is considered a separate source, Having its own usage and only being activatable when in the corresponding form. You may be concentrating on multiple forms at the same time, at the start of your turn select one of your forms to use its size, composition and defense class until your next turn. When concentrating on multiple forms, you may use any of those forms abilities regardless of which forms size you select. When concentrating on multiple forms, your extra forms do not grant you the ability to concentrate on extra effects per form.","When you pick this, choose different skill proficiencies for your form. You enter your form for the rest of the scene {Half points} times per Story, gaining one of the below effects.\nTerrifying: When you Succeed on an attack, or succeed a check to harm or destroy things, cause nearby civilians to flee in terror.\nLurking: If you haven't been seen in your form, you have advantage on conceal checks. Otherwise you gain +1 to conceal.\nAlluring: You have a +1 to convince results.","Next situation, you have advantage on concentrating on your form.","Next situation, you have disadvantage on concentrating on your form.","{Power}",B.p7,!1,null,null,B.a5a,"{1}")
B.ahB=new A.cw("source_gadgets","Gadgets","The character gains their powers from created objects. Every combat feature is a unique object or a part in another unique object, that can appear as anything but has the properties of a single Implement selected when you take the feature. When you use the gadget, you have a source value of {Power + 1}. You may use the gadget once, then you must fix the gadget to use it again. If multiple features are in the same object, each feature can be used and fixed independently.\nFix: [Action] fix all of your Gadgets.\nJerryRig: [Reaction] During your or allies turn, you may spend your reaction and fix 1 gadget.","For each of your gadgets, You may gain advantage or +1 on results on a skill check. You may not do this again with this gadget until you either make a skill check with disadvantage or -1 to results.","Choose 1 of your gadgets and the first time you activate it in the next situation, you don't need to fix it.","Randomly choose 1 of your gadgets; it starts the next situation requiring a fix before you can use it.","{Power + 1}",B.p8,!1,null,null,B.f1,null)
B.ahw=new A.cw("source_granted_power","Granted Power","The character gets their features from a powerful entity. They may use their powers {2 * points} times per story. They regain all uses after each story. Your source value is {Power + 1}. Abilities of this source require the use of an implement.","You have {2 * points} blessings per Story. When you fail a skill check, you may pay 1 blessing to reroll. At the end of a situation or combat encounter, regain all your blessings.","Regain {points / 2} granted power usages.","Whenever you use a granted power usage, make a Vit defense; on problems suffer {vitality d6} damage.","{Power + 1}",B.F0,!0,null,null,B.f1,null)
B.F1=new A.mq(3,"heat")
B.ahK=new A.bp("Shield","Target you and allies range {Power}, and Gain {half points d6} shield.",!1)
B.ahY=new A.bp("Burning","Target Enemies range {Power} and give them {half points d6} Burn. Pick the damage type and target when you pick this.",!1)
B.ahX=new A.bp("Growing","Each time you overload, increase the damage done by all attacks of this overload by 1d6, to a max bonus of {Power + points /3 d6}.",!1)
B.ahO=new A.bp("Warp","Target you and allies range {Power} and teleport each target to a free space within {Half points +1}.",!1)
B.aif=new A.bp("Combat Feature","Select a Combat Feature and trigger that as an overload effect using a source value of {Half Power + Half points}.",!0)
B.a48=s([B.ahK,B.ahY,B.ahX,B.ahO,B.aif],t.AJ)
B.ahF=new A.cw("source_heat","Heat","The character gains their power through a slowly growing process, like a steam engine, or channeling spirit, or eating a big sandwich. Whenever you use an ability of this source, you gain 1 heat up to {Power + 1} and then do the ability using your heat as the source. When you would gain a heat but are at the max, instead you gain an overheat effect, and after you perform the ability, set your heat to 0. You pick the overheat effect when you pick the feature. Each overheat effect is a separate source. Features of the same overheat effect share heat, and you track each overheat effects heat levels separately.","During a situation, before making a roll you may warm up making the check with a -1 to the results. After warming up, for the rest of the situation you make that skill check with a +1 to results.","Start the next situation at {Half Power} heat.","The first time you would overheat in the next situation, instead set your heat to {Half Power}.","{1}",B.F1,!1,null,"{Power + 1}",B.a48,"{1}")
B.p6=new A.mq(1,"resource")
B.ahD=new A.cw("source_intuitive_magic","Intuitive Magic","The caster can freely cast their magic. You require an implement to use this source. They have {3 * Power * points} Max MP that they regain at the start of each Story. When they use a feature they must spend at least 1 MP and may spend up to {Power + Half Power} MP using a feature as the Source Value. On problems with an attack or status check, you pay only 1 MP.","You may spend 2 MP to gain advantage on a skill or defense check. If multiple characters are making the same check, you may spend 1 MP per character to give them advantage.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Intuitive Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","1",B.p6,!0,"MP","{3 * Power * points}",B.f1,null)
B.ahz=new A.cw("source_prepared_magic","Prepared Magic","The caster can only cast magic that they have prepared in advance. You require an implement to use this source. They have {3 * Power * points} Max MP and start every Story with Full MP. Whenever they gain points of features, they may pick an equal number of points of features to form their spellbook. After each encounter, the character may prepare uses of their Prepared Magic features, choosing features with the source and features in their spellbook and the amount of MP spent to Prepare the Spell. Each prepared spell uses the MP spent as the Source value. Prepared spells must spend at least 1 MP, and no more than {1+Power} MP. You may prepare as many uses of any features in your spellbook that you can pay for. You may prepare the same feature multiple times.","You may have up to a total of {points} prepared skill spells per story. For each preparation, pick a skill; you may change what you have prepared at the end of a situation. When you perform a skill check, you may use a prepared skill to gain advantage. Your prepared skill spells are objects you can give to your allies to use as well.","Regain {Power * points / 4} MP.","-1 on checks made from Prepared Magic abilities, and on problems, instead pay the full amount of MP.","MP Spent",B.p6,!0,"MP","{3 * Power * points}",B.f1,null)
B.hx=new A.mq(2,"resourceWithSelection")
B.ai8=new A.bp("Flow","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki point to Ready, Run or Retreat after the ability.",!1)
B.ahI=new A.bp("Flurry","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to make 1 Melee Attack targeting an enemy range 1. On success, deal {Power d6}. Choose the defense targeted when you pick this.",!1)
B.aii=new A.bp("Restore","During your turn, You may spend 1 Ki Point to gain {Half Level d12} Regeneration.",!1)
B.aij=new A.bp("Breath","Before you would make an Int, Wis, or Cha defense, you may pay 1 Ki to gain advantage on the roll.",!1)
B.ai3=new A.bp("Meditative","After you fail a concentration, spend 1 ki point and succeed instead.",!1)
B.ait=new A.bp("Present","You fail with a ki attack, you may spend a ki point to reroll the attack.",!1)
B.a4V=s([B.ai8,B.ahI,B.aii,B.aij,B.ai3,B.ait],t.AJ)
B.ahE=new A.cw("source_ki","Ki","The character gains their powers from controlling their body's energy called ki. For each point spent on this source, the character gains 2 ki points, regaining all at the end of every situation. A character can activate their features using 1 ki point using a source of {Half Power} and they may trigger one of their ki effects. For every 2 points spent on this source, gain 1 of the below options.","You may pay 2 ki to reroll a skill you are proficient in one time.","Start the next situation with {Half points} extra Ki.","When you trigger a Ki effect, you must succeed a Vit Defense or lose the ki point without gaining a benefit from the effect.","{Half Power}",B.hx,!1,"Ki","{2 * points}",B.a4V,"{points / 2}")
B.ais=new A.bp("Buzzed","Gain resistance to the damage of the next {Vitality} attacks that hit you. You may not have more than {Vice + Vitality} stacks of this.",!1)
B.ahM=new A.bp("Angry","This round, you deal extra damage equal to your concentration roll on all attacks or damaging status checks.",!1)
B.aig=new A.bp("Friendly","You may make a status check vs cha, on success, pull an enemy {Vice + Vitality}. You may instead target an ally and force them to move the same distance as you would have pulled an enemy.",!1)
B.ai7=new A.bp("Against Enemies","You and your allies gain +1 to attacks against enemies adjacent to your specter.",!1)
B.ai0=new A.bp("From Enemies","You and your allies gain +1 to defenses against attacks from enemies adjacent to your specter.",!1)
B.auz=s([B.ai7,B.ai0],t.AJ)
B.aia=new A.bp("Regretful","Target a free space within {Half Vice + Half Vitality} up to your Vice Pts and summon a specter of your regrets that last until you activate this again or die.\nSpecters block their space, use your defenses, and you take half damage dealt to your specter ignoring shield and resistance.",!1)
B.a3k=s([B.ais,B.ahM,B.aig,B.aia],t.AJ)
B.ahx=new A.cw("source_vice","Vice","The character gains their power through a self destructive vice, like drinking or stamp collecting. At the start of your turn, you may consume your vice taking {level + Vitality} damage vs Vit and gaining {Power} vice. You may have up to {2 * power} vice and it is lost at the end of the encounter. You can spend up to {Power} vice to use an ability, with spent vice + 1 as the source value; you may pay the vice health cost again to not pay the vice. When you pick this the first time, pick a below option that triggers when you consume your vice at the start of your turn.","Choose either Convince or Conceal. You may take your vice during a situation to gain a +1 to results of all skills other than the selected skill and disadvantage on the selected skill.","Reduce your vice health cost by {Half Vitality}.","At the start of your turn, make a Wis defense, or you must consume your vice.","{Power}",B.hx,!1,"Vice","{2 * power}",B.a3k,"{1}")
B.aik=new A.bp("Sprint","During your turn, you may pay stamina to move extra spaces. You move up to 2 spaces further for each stamina spent. This doesn't alter your speed. Whenever you are under an effect that reduces your speed, you move 1 space per stamina instead.",!1)
B.ail=new A.bp("Dodge Roll","Before rolling a defense, you may spend {Vitality} stamina to gain advantage on the defense.",!1)
B.aic=new A.bp("Follow through","On success with an attack that deals damage, you may spend up to {Half Power} stamina to deal 1d6 extra damage per stamina spent.",!1)
B.ahQ=new A.bp("Leap","[Reaction] During your turn or at the end of an ally\u2019s turn, [Reaction] and Pay up to {Vitality} stamina, and dash to a free space within 2 * paid stamina.",!1)
B.ain=new A.bp("Stretch","Once per ability, you may pay 1 stamina to increase your range by 1.",!1)
B.a4F=s([B.aik,B.ail,B.aic,B.ahQ,B.ain],t.AJ)
B.ahC=new A.cw("source_stamina","Stamina","The character gains their power through their physical endurance and strength. The character has {Power * points} Max Stamina, and regains all stamina at the end of the encounter. When they use a feature of this source, they may spend up to {Power} stamina, using the spent stamina as the source value. Breath: At the end of the round, if they haven't spent stamina this round, they gain {Power + Vitality} Stamina. For every 4 pts worth of combat features of the stamina source, gain 1 of the below abilities. You always know at least 1.","You may pay {half power} stamina to reroll a defense with a +1 to the result. You start the next encounter without this stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you Breath, regain {points / 3} extra stamina.","During the next situation, whenever you breathe, regain half the stamina.","{Power}",B.hx,!1,"Stamina","{Power * points}",B.a4F,"{points / 4}")
B.ahy=new A.cw("source_mutation","Mutation","You gain your powers from your body's ability to reorganize itself.\nEvolution: You have a Genepool of {points} combat features you select when you gain pts. You have {points} Evolution points at the start of every encounter. On your turn, You may spend evolution points to gain access to a feature in your genepool as a mutation. You may use the mutation for the remainder of the encounter with a source of {Half Power}. Mutations cost as many evolution points as they would feature points, and you may pay for upgrades up to the normal limit. You have a morph pool of {points / 3} Universal upgrades, and you may only use universal upgrades from your morph pool when you upgrade a mutation. When you trigger a mutation on later turns, you may pay for upgrades if possible. You may not exceed the normal feature upgrade limits. You must have a mutation to be able to use an ability in your genepool. You may pay twice the evolution cost of a mutation to give the mutation a source value of {Power} instead of {Half Power}.\nMutating Ability: When combined with another source, mutations are tracked per ability, Divide the points as whole points between the sources of the ability. When you use the ability as a Mutation, before activating, you may change a number of upgrades up to the Mutation points of this ability. When you activate the ability via mutation, use a source value of {Half Power}.","{points / 3} times per Story, you may change your skill proficiencies or armor & fortitude values before making a check. This remains for the rest of the scene.","During the next situation: After activating a mutation ability, lose the mutation and regain those evolution points.","During the next situation, you reduce your max evolution points by 1.","{Half Power}",B.p7,!1,null,null,B.f1,null)
B.F2=new A.mq(4,"time")
B.ahG=new A.cw("source_time","Time","The character gains their power through altering time or predicting the future. After each encounter, you may select your chronomancy from 1 to {half points}. Your time source is {power - chronomancy}. At the start of a story, Roll and record {Chronomancy +1} attacks and {Chronomancy +1} skills you are proficient in. When you use this source you use one of your applicable chronomancy results, then roll a replacement result.\nYour chronomancy results don't benefit from +1 or -1 to success. Whenever you have advantage or disadvantage, select 1 result then roll the extra check. If you gain a reroll, reroll as normal. When you change your chronomancy at the end of a situation, you pick which results are lost, and you only make new rolls for gained chronomancy. You may use an Implement gaining any implement effects. If you do, you require that type of implement to use the feature.","When you make a skill check you have a recorded result for, you may use one of your applicable chronomancy results instead of rolling, then roll a replacement result.","Reroll half of your chronomancy results.","Set half of your chronomancy results to 1.","{power - chronomancy}",B.F2,!0,"Chronomancy",null,B.f1,null)
B.aim=new A.bp("Penetration","Pay 1 Psi Point and your ability ignores resistance.",!1)
B.aiu=new A.bp("Drain","On Success, Pay up to {Half power} Additional Psi Points, to deal 1d6 extra damage and gain an equal amount of shield per Psi Point.",!1)
B.ahV=new A.bp("Focus","Pay 1 Psi Point, and attacks ignore advantage, disadvantage, -1 and +1 to results for the attack and defenses caused by the attack.",!1)
B.ahL=new A.bp("Distant","Pay 1 Psi Point and double the range of the ability or if the ability targets an area, increase the area size and range by 1.",!1)
B.ai2=new A.bp("Phasing","Pay 1 Psi Point, and your movement doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity and you ignore difficult terrain.",!1)
B.a6o=s([B.aim,B.aiu,B.ahV,B.ahL,B.ai2],t.AJ)
B.ahA=new A.cw("source_psionics","Psionics","The character uses their mind to alter reality. They have {3 * Power * points} Max Psi Points, regaining half after each encounter. When using a feature, They must spend at least 1 Psi Point and may spend up to {Power} Psi Points as the Source Value, and they may trigger one of their psi powers. They pick {points / 4} psi powers. You may use an Implement gaining any implement effects. If you do, you require that type of implement to use the feature.","You may spend 2 Psi Points to gain advantage on a skill you are proficient in or an Int, Wis, or Cha defense check. If a character you can see is making a skill check that you have proficiency in, you may spend 1 Psi Point and that character rolls using your skill rather than their own.","Regain {Power} Psi Points.","-1 on checks made from Psionic abilities, and to trigger any of your Psi Powers you must make and succeed on a Defense vs Int first.","Psi Points Spent",B.hx,!0,"Psi Points","{3 * Power * points}",B.a6o,"{points / 4}")
